 format(2000); // "2s"
 ```
 
+### Compound Durations
+
+Use `parseCompound` to total several parts in one string. Parts can be separated by spaces, by a comma, or not at all.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days, 4 hours'); // 187200000
+parseCompound('1h30m'); // 5400000
+```
+
+Unlike `parse`, which returns `NaN` for invalid input, `parseCompound` throws a `TypeError`. When there is more than one part, each part needs a unit.
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
